From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lophinya <lophinya@localhost>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 00:25:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime access guard + restore Bukkit async  scheduler

Folia replaces CraftScheduler.handle with an unconditional, message-less throw.
Two problems with that, addressed separately and both switchable:

1. Diagnostics. The bare UnsupportedOperationException names the plugin class and
   nothing else. LophinyaSchedulerDiagnostics logs plugin name+version, jar file
   and SHA-256, the Bukkit scheduler method actually called, delay/period, the
   sync/async flag, the plugin callsite, and the thread/region context - once per
   distinct callsite. Behaviour is unchanged; the call still throws.
   Kill switch: -Dlophinya.compat.diagnostics=false

2. Async reach. Folia's throw also killed the async path, which never needed a
   main thread - Paper already runs those on CraftAsyncScheduler's own pool.
   Restoring that delegation is a return to Paper semantics, not a compatibility
   shim, and async tasks that illegally touch world state are still caught by
   Folia's thread-ownership checks. Folia commented out the per-tick
   mainThreadHeartbeat, so the async scheduler's clock is driven from
   FoliaGlobalRegionScheduler.tick() - counter only, no plugin code runs there.
   Sync tasks are still rejected, deliberately.
   Kill switch: -Dlophinya.compat.restoreAsyncScheduler=false

Hardening round (probe2 suite, 2026-07-27) found and fixed two bugs the async
restore made reachable:

3. Cancellation. cancelTask(int)/cancelTasks(Plugin) performed the async-side
   cancel and then died on the sync-side bookkeeping guard task, which goes
   through handle() and throws under regionised threading. Callers of
   BukkitTask.cancel() got an UnsupportedOperationException after the cancel had
   already taken effect (probe2: 3/3 cancel paths threw pre-fix, 0/3 post-fix).
   The sync queues can never contain plugin tasks here, so the bookkeeping is
   skipped instead of throwing. Gated on the same kill switch.

4. Plugin disable. Folia removed getScheduler().cancelTasks(plugin) from
   PaperPluginInstanceManager.disablePlugin, so a disabled plugin's restored
   async timers kept running its code forever (probe2 buddy plugin: 55 fires
   after onDisable, right up to server shutdown). The call is restored behind
   the same kill switch, matching Paper's disable semantics.

diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
index 455e8c24d98fcd0ae0a349737a0e709a05ed9170..1b54ac91e6a34dbc51fa4ccacd7934fc0c85c1c5 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
@@ -260,6 +260,19 @@ class PaperPluginInstanceManager {
         }
 
         // Folia - region threading
+        // Lophinya start - restored async scheduler: cancel Bukkit tasks on disable, like Paper does
+        // Folia removed this call because CraftScheduler was fully disabled. With the async path
+        // restored (patch 0024), a disabled plugin's async timers would otherwise keep running its
+        // code forever - the exact bug this call exists to prevent on Paper.
+        if (fun.bm.lecithin.config.modules.CompatConfig.restoreAsyncScheduler) {
+            try {
+                this.server.getScheduler().cancelTasks(plugin);
+            } catch (Throwable ex) {
+                this.handlePluginException("Error occurred (in the plugin loader) while cancelling tasks for "
+                    + pluginName + " (Is it up to date?)", ex, plugin); // Paper
+            }
+        }
+        // Lophinya end - restored async scheduler: cancel Bukkit tasks on disable, like Paper does
 
         // Paper start - Folia schedulers
         try {
diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/scheduler/FoliaGlobalRegionScheduler.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/scheduler/FoliaGlobalRegionScheduler.java
index f20f2735fbb4d1e38d576eafe18a0054a45aa59e..0010c331243d95f1506bc9fed7ddc5644c6e4927 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/scheduler/FoliaGlobalRegionScheduler.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/scheduler/FoliaGlobalRegionScheduler.java
@@ -20,6 +20,19 @@ public class FoliaGlobalRegionScheduler implements GlobalRegionScheduler {
     private final Object stateLockForTaskId = new Object(); // Lophine - add task id
 
     public void tick() {
+        // Lophinya start - drive the restored Bukkit async scheduler off the global tick
+        // Folia commented out MinecraftServer's per-tick mainThreadHeartbeat(), which is what used to
+        // advance CraftAsyncScheduler's clock. Without this, restored async tasks would be accepted
+        // and then never fire. Only the async scheduler's counter is advanced here; no plugin code
+        // runs on the global tick thread as a result.
+        if (fun.bm.lecithin.config.modules.CompatConfig.restoreAsyncScheduler) {
+            final org.bukkit.scheduler.BukkitScheduler bukkitScheduler = org.bukkit.Bukkit.getScheduler();
+            if (bukkitScheduler instanceof org.bukkit.craftbukkit.scheduler.CraftScheduler craftScheduler) {
+                craftScheduler.lophinya$asyncHeartbeat();
+            }
+        }
+        // Lophinya end - drive the restored Bukkit async scheduler off the global tick
+
         final List<GlobalScheduledTask> run;
         synchronized (this.stateLock) {
             ++this.tickCount;
diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
index c4dcddc4db02ed3641d05fae31ead7c13205f841..f5d23194f7c6d7c9de3b01c396ca8df9816833d8 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
@@ -273,6 +273,15 @@ public class CraftScheduler implements BukkitScheduler {
         if (task != null) {
             task.cancel0();
         }
+        // Lophinya start - restored async scheduler: cancellation must not die on sync-side bookkeeping
+        // The guard task below goes through handle(), which regionised threading rejects - the caller
